Osmium UI's own code is released into the public domain under the
Unlicense (see LICENSE): the TypeScript and CSS, the Swift window host,
the TrueType writer and the bitmap font encoding, and the four arrow
glyphs (U+2190..2193) added to Charcoal 12 and Geneva 10.

The Unlicense does not cover the Mac OS 8 material that Osmium UI
reproduces. These bitmaps were captured or redrawn pixel for pixel from
Apple's Mac OS 8.0 and 8.5 screen output, from the Mac OS 8 Human
Interface Guidelines (1997) and from Mac OS 8.0's Appearance Extension:

- the Charcoal 12 and Geneva 12, 10 and 9 bitmap strikes in src/fonts/,
  from which installOsmium() builds browser fonts at run time;
- the alert icons in src/alertsprites.ts;
- the control bitmaps in src/controlsprites.ts;
- the window sprites in src/sprites.ts.

